{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/c19u5a","slideIndex":1,"text":"25 seconds. PM2.5 is fine particulate matter. Our output is concentration in micrograms per cubic metre at a future station hour. We ask whether learned patterns improve on simply repeating the latest reading. The project also addresses a practical problem: public data can arrive late and contain gaps. Its scope is individual stations, so it cannot establish a citywide exposure or health alert."}
