{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/yqq1b9","slideIndex":5,"text":"30 seconds. Ridge gives a fast linear comparison after scaling. XGBoost can learn nonlinear feature combinations. We compare a small fixed search and minimize validation MAE. PCP 31 selects 350 trees with depth five at each horizon. Persistence repeats the origin value. Same hour yesterday refers to the target hour on the previous day. At a 24-hour horizon it is identical to persistence, so it is not a second independent next-day baseline.\n\nSources: backend/train_current.py; https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.02754; https://otexts.com/fpp3/simple-methods.html"}
