{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/4iec0s","slideIndex":6,"text":"35 seconds. These are PCP 31 test results. At six hours XGBoost MAE is 6.33 against 9.18 for persistence, an approximately 31 percent reduction. One-hour MAE is 2.94 and next-day MAE is 7.12. We compare on identical eligible rows within each horizon. The table of uncertainty on a later slide explains why the six-hour improvement has stronger evidence than the other two.\n\nSources: artifacts/current/test_metrics.csv"}
