{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/rh3sdu","slideIndex":8,"text":"40 seconds. These rows compare the same model with persistence on specific next-day groups. On historical peaks, XGBoost loses despite its overall gain. At PCP 31, sparse weekly history gives MAE 5.17 versus 2.44, and spring gives 4.30 versus 3.05. Different rows are different subgroups and stations, not directly comparable exposure regimes. PCP 31 also underpredicts its high-concentration group with mean bias minus 20.56. We cannot attribute these errors to weather because weather is absent.\n\nSources: artifacts/peak_errors.csv; artifacts/current/analysis/sparse_history_errors.csv; artifacts/current/analysis/season_errors.csv; artifacts/current/analysis/peak_errors.csv"}
