{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/le00tw","slideIndex":9,"text":"35 seconds. We pair model and baseline errors and resample seven-day blocks 2000 times. Nineteen blocks contain eligible observations. Only the six-hour interval excludes zero. These are approximate intervals for aggregate MAE improvement, not bounds around tomorrow’s concentration. There are no eligible summer examples and only three October next-day examples. We therefore cannot claim year-round or current-condition reliability.\n\nSources: artifacts/current/analysis/paired_block_bootstrap.csv; artifacts/current/analysis/recent_period_errors.csv; artifacts/current/analysis/season_errors.csv"}
