{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ws78at","slideIndex":10,"text":"30 seconds. This screenshot shows the recorded 10 October demonstration. The app uses React and TypeScript with a FastAPI backend. Refresh retrieves measurements and reruns the saved pipelines. The target date starts from the measured hour. A next-day point can therefore appear, but it is not an arbitrary future-date forecast. Daily and weekly counts show the input context. If publication delays make the input stale, the app warns users and labels expired target hours.\n\nSources: latest-forecast-preview.jpg; backend/app/current.py; frontend/src/App.tsx"}
