{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/5yuzq1","slideIndex":11,"text":"30 seconds. Reproduce mode verifies the immutable dataset hash and uses the recorded station, settings and chronological boundaries. It works independently of today’s date. Update mode downloads fresh data and applies station freshness checks, saving a new experiment without automatically replacing deployed models. Our repeated run matches the saved predictions and metrics. We conclude that six-hour forecasts are useful in the held-out evidence, while peaks and sparse history require further work. Weather features, calibrated prediction intervals and fallback rules need a new evaluation period.\n\nSources: backend/train_current.py; backend/tests/test_training_modes.py; artifacts/reproduce/verified-run/test_metrics.csv; README.md"}
