{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/l9nyls","slideIndex":12,"text":"Use this slide after the six-minute talk, then switch to the app at http://127.0.0.1:8000/. Minute 0 to 1: latest station identity, origin time and 24/168-hour coverage. Minute 1 to 2: target cards, the next-day target and a past target if applicable. Minute 2 to 3: refresh, explain inference versus retraining, and export CSV. If refresh fails, explain the saved-data warning rather than claiming fresh data. Minute 3 to 4: historical replay, choose a valid 2024 origin and reveal observed outcomes. Minute 4 to 5: station directory, distinguish reporting stations from the trained station and explain reproducibility. Keep the recorded screenshot as fallback for a network outage.\n\nSources: README.md; frontend/src/App.tsx; backend/app/current.py"}
