{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/cjan7o","slideIndex":13,"text":"Use during the three-minute question period. Why XGBoost? It won the fixed validation comparison; no claim against untested model families. Why no future date picker? The estimator predicts only the trained horizons after the latest observed origin, and requires real historical inputs. Why not trust the average MAE? Peaks, spring and sparse-history groups can lose to persistence. Does the model use live measurements? It uses the latest published public snapshot, with delays and missingness displayed. Contribution question: explain your actual implementation and analysis work, and disclose AI assistance according to your course policy.\n\nSources: MODEL_FAILURES.md; README.md"}
